    "badgeClassName": "a2-paper",
    "emoji": "📌",
    "category": "Poisson Distribution",
    "weightBadge": "S2",
    "topics": [
      "\\(X\\sim\\text{Po}(\\lambda)\\)",
      "\\(P(X=r)=e^{-\\lambda}\\lambda^r/r!\\)",
      "Mean = Var = \\(\\lambda\\)",
      "Poisson approx. to Binomial"
    ]
  },
  "content": {
    "blocks": [
      {
        "kind": "topicGrid",
        "items": [
          {
            "title": "Conditions",
            "body": "Events occur independently, at a constant average rate \\(\\lambda\\), and singly in time/space. \\(X\\sim\\text{Po}(\\lambda)\\)."
          },
          {
            "title": "Probability Formula",
            "body": "\\(P(X=r)=\\dfrac{e^{-\\lambda}\\lambda^r}{r!}\\) for \\(r=0,1,2,\\ldots\\)"
          },
          {
            "title": "Mean and Variance",
            "body": "\\(E(X)=\\text{Var}(X)=\\lambda\\). The mean equals the variance — a key identifying feature."
          },
          {
            "title": "Cumulative Tables",
            "body": "Use Poisson tables for \\(P(X\\leq r)\\). Note \\(P(X\\geq r)=1-P(X\\leq r-1)\\). Additive: \\(X+Y\\sim\\text{Po}(\\lambda_1+\\lambda_2)\\)."
          },
          {
            "title": "Changing the Interval",
            "body": "If \\(X\\sim\\text{Po}(\\lambda)\\) per hour, then in \\(t\\) hours: \\(X\\sim\\text{Po}(\\lambda t)\\)."
          },
          {
            "title": "Normal Approximation",
            "body": "If \\(\\lambda&gt;15\\): \\(\\text{Po}(\\lambda)\\approx N(\\lambda,\\lambda)\\) with continuity correction."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "kind": "callout",
        "style": "thm",
        "label": {
          "en": "▲ Poisson Distribution — Reference",
          "ar": null
        },
        "body": {
          "en": "If events occur at a constant average rate \\(\\lambda\\) independently, \\(X\\sim\\text{Po}(\\lambda)\\) with:\n          \\(P(X=r)=\\dfrac{e^{-\\lambda}\\lambda^r}{r!}\\) for \\(r=0,1,2,\\ldots\\) &nbsp;·&nbsp; \\(E(X)=\\lambda\\), \\(\\text{Var}(X)=\\lambda\\).\n          <strong>Poisson approximation to Binomial:</strong> if \\(n\\) is large, \\(p\\) is small, \\(np=\\lambda\\) is moderate (\\(n&gt;50, p&lt;0.1\\)), then \\(B(n,p)\\approx\\text{Po}(\\lambda)\\).",
          "ar": null
        }
      },
      {
        "kind": "cards",
        "items": [
          {
            "label": {
              "en": "\\(P(X=r)\\)",
              "ar": null
            },
            "value": {
              "en": "\\(\\dfrac{e^{-\\lambda}\\lambda^r}{r!}\\)",
              "ar": null
            }
          },
          {
            "label": {
              "en": "Mean = Var",
              "ar": null
            },
            "value": {
              "en": "\\(\\lambda\\)",
              "ar": null
            }
          },
          {
            "label": {
              "en": "Sum of Poissons",
              "ar": null
            },
            "value": {
              "en": "\\(X+Y\\sim\\text{Po}(\\lambda_1+\\lambda_2)\\)",
              "ar": null
            }
          },
          {
            "label": {
              "en": "Binom approx",
              "ar": null
            },
            "value": {
              "en": "\\(n&gt;50,\\,p&lt;0.1,\\,\\lambda=np\\)",
              "ar": null
            }
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "kind": "callout",
        "style": "example",
        "label": {
          "en": "Worked example — Exact probability",
          "ar": null
        },
        "body": {
          "en": "<p>Faults in a wire occur at a rate of 2 per metre. Find the probability of (a) exactly 3 faults in 1 m, (b) fewer than 2 faults in 0.5 m.</p><p>(a) \\(\\lambda=2\\): \\(P(X=3)=\\dfrac{e^{-2}\\cdot8}{6}\\approx0.1804\\).</p><p>(b) \\(\\lambda=1\\): \\(P(X&lt;2)=P(0)+P(1)=e^{-1}+e^{-1}=2e^{-1}\\approx0.7358\\).</p>",
          "ar": null
        }
      },
      {
        "kind": "callout",
        "style": "example",
        "label": {
          "en": "Worked example — Binomial approximation",
          "ar": null
        },
        "body": {
          "en": "<p>\\(X\\sim B(200,0.02)\\). Use a Poisson approximation to find \\(P(X=5)\\).</p><p>\\(\\lambda=200\\times0.02=4\\). \\(P(X=5)=\\dfrac{e^{-4}\\cdot4^5}{120}=\\dfrac{1024e^{-4}}{120}\\approx0.1563\\).</p>",
          "ar": null
        }
      },
      {
        "kind": "practiceProblem",
        "question": {
          "en": "Cars arrive at a toll booth at an average rate of 3 per minute. Find the probability that (a) exactly 5 arrive in one minute, (b) at least 2 arrive in 30 seconds.",
          "ar": null
        },
        "solution": {
          "en": "(a) \\(P(X=5)=\\dfrac{e^{-3}\\cdot243}{120}\\approx0.1008\\). (b) \\(\\lambda=1.5\\): \\(P(X\\geq2)=1-P(0)-P(1)=1-e^{-1.5}-1.5e^{-1.5}=1-2.5e^{-1.5}\\approx0.4422\\).",
          "ar": null
        }
      },
